## Merge upstream release v0.9.2 into integration-latest

Context:
Upstream OntoBricks v0.9.2 (tag c671fef2) adds multiple UC datasets per class
(tables, views and metric views, #221), MCP end-user identity forwarding past
the Apps proxy (#208), domain-scoped MCP tools without a sticky session
(#209), typed SPARQL value FILTERs compiled to SQL (#210), the
user_api_scopes cleanup, uv-provisioned CPython in setup, and refreshed
dependency locks. #208/#209/#210 and the scope cleanup were already
cherry-picked here, so most of the overlap resolved to upstream's version.

Conflict resolutions:
1. databricks.yml
   - Upstream comments kept. UI app keeps `user_api_scopes: [sql, files]`
     (Knowledge Store UC Volume import), MCP app `[sql]`. One key per app.
2. app.yaml.template
   - Kept the note that scopes live in databricks.yml; the `authorization`
     block upstream re-adds is ignored by bundle deploys and listing only
     `sql` there would contradict the UI app's `files` scope.
3. docs/deployment.md
   - Kept our paragraph (it also documents the `files` scope).
4. src/mcp-server/server/session.py
   - Took upstream (#209 final form plus the `datasets` list). The MCP
     server tree is now identical to v0.9.2.
   - Kept our src/agents/tools/loopback_http.py raw-bytes header handling
     for non-ASCII display names (upstream has no equivalent).
5. src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
   - Upstream multi-dataset picker ("Already linked" note) combined with our
     `data-i18n-skip` on the asset name.
6. tests/units/settings/test_bundle_job_resource.py
   - Kept our exact-scope tests and added upstream's subset test.
7. changelogs/v0.9.2/benoitcayladbx_2026-10-30.log (add/add)
   - Upstream file as-is; our notes stay under changelogs/v0.9.1/.

Adaptations:
1. src/back/objects/mapping/MetricViewBindings.py
   - `resolve()` takes an optional `linked` map (class URI -> linked dataset
     names). The mapping remains the source of truth: a class-linked metric
     view the mapping does not read never creates `derivedFrom`.
   - When a mapping reads several metric views exposing the column, a view
     linked to the class wins; otherwise the explicit table, then the SQL
     sources in order. Duplicate sources are dropped.
2. src/back/objects/ontology/definitions/DefinitionReferences.py
   - New `linked_datasets()` reads `datasets` and the legacy `dataset` via
     `ClassModel.normalize_datasets` and feeds it to `reconcile()`.
3. src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py, OntologyParser.py
   - Upstream's module-level `ClassModel` import made back.core.w3c import
     back.objects at package load; importing agents.agent_dtwin_chat first
     then failed with a circular import. The import is now local to the two
     methods that use it (class sizes stay within the architecture baseline).
4. src/front/static/global/js/i18n-ko.js
   - Korean entries for the new dataset picker / panel / preview strings.
5. tests/units/definitions/test_metric_view_bindings_multi_dataset.py (new)
   - Linked-dataset extraction (list and legacy shape), table + metric view
     on one class, linked view not read by the mapping, two-view tie-break,
     reconcile end to end.

Modified files (on top of the upstream merge):
- app.yaml.template, databricks.yml, docs/deployment.md
- changelogs/v0.9.2/simyung-yang_2026-11-09.log (new)
- src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyGenerator.py
- src/back/core/w3c/owl/OntologyParser.py
- src/back/objects/mapping/MetricViewBindings.py
- src/back/objects/ontology/definitions/DefinitionReferences.py
- src/front/static/global/js/i18n-ko.js
- src/front/static/ontology/js/ontology-shared-panels.js
- src/mcp-server/server/session.py
- tests/units/definitions/test_metric_view_bindings_multi_dataset.py (new)
- tests/units/settings/test_bundle_job_resource.py

